    "abstract": "Parts list for the aft fuselage sill frames between stations C52 and C66, covering the frame ribs, the lower intercostals, the stiffeners and the fastener set that attaches them to the lower shell, with the frame foot bolt grip taken from the common stack table.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the detail parts of the aft fuselage sill frames between stations C52 and C66, including the loading rail reaction bracket land.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand side looking outboard and sheet 2 the right-hand side, which is symmetric except at the loading rail reaction bracket where the left-hand side carries an additional stiffener. Item numbers run forward to aft. The fastener quantities given are per frame bay, not per aircraft. The frame ribs are supplied as machined items and are not interchangeable between the two aircraft types because the frame pitch differs. Item 90 is listed at the grip length for the bare frame foot only. Where the foot is picked up by the inner doubler of the longitudinal skin joint, the stack is one increment thicker and the grip length is read from the stack table on sheet 2 of FIG-53-31-12-01, which is the governing table for both figures; a kit made up from the bare-foot length alone will be short at every doubler position."
    },
